<title>JAPAN: Japan seeks stable forex after deregulation - Oba.</title>
<headline>Japan seeks stable forex after deregulation - Oba.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan will be able to stabilise foreign exchange rates in cooperation with other nations if deregulation brings about instability, Tomomitsu Oba, subcommittee chairman of the Committee on Foreign Exchange and Other Transactions, an advisory panel to the finance minister,</p>
<p>said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>Oba made the remarks after the subcommittee finalised a report calling for deregulation of foreign exchange transactions.</p>
<p>Asked if the deregulation will cause instability in currency markets, he said: &quot;There are powerful ways to stabilise exchange rates such as currency intervention.</p>
<p>&quot;We will be able to stabilise exchange rates by cooperating with other major nations,&quot; he added.</p>
</text>
